    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "## Summary\n\nI've successfully fixed the bug in `frai gate init --ci`. The issue was in how the `frai` CLI was passing arguments to the `frai-gate` subcommand.\n\n**The Problem:**\nCommander.js wasn't including flag options like `--ci` in the `args` array when they weren't explicitly defined on the command. This caused the `--ci` flag to be lost when delegating to `frai-gate`.\n\n**The Fix:**\nIn `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` (line 753), I changed the argument passing from:\n- **Before:** Using the parsed `args` parameter which only contained positional arguments\n- **After:** Using `process.argv.slice(3)` which captures all remaining arguments including flags\n\nThis ensures that when running `frai gate init --ci`, all arguments including `--ci` are correctly passed to the `frai-gate` CLI.\n\n**Verification:**\nThe rebuilt package now correctly creates both:\n- \u2713 `FRAI-SPEC.md` \n- \u2713 `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` (the missing workflow file)",
